--   Represent the eight compositions $1234$, $1\mid234$, $12\mid34$, $123\mid4$, $1\mid2\mid34$, $1\mid23\mid4$, $12\mid3\mid4$, and $1\mid2\mid3\mid4$ by their explicit block families. For an arbitrary rational signed weight function $w$ on these eight objects, define
--
--   $$(Aw)_B=\sum_P w(P)\mathbf1_{\{B\in P\}}.$$
--
--   The sum is the explicit eight-term block-incidence evaluation. Define $\sigma$ to be $+1$ on $12\mid34$ and the discrete composition, $-1$ on $1\mid2\mid34$ and $12\mid3\mid4$, and zero on the other four objects. These definitions specify the map and the proposed kernel direction for the four-label classification. No nonnegativity or probability normalization is imposed on $w$. The bundle uses this fixed eight-constructor representation; it does not itself construct an equivalence with the general endpoint-certified partition representation.
